## Forge workflow

This repository's primary forge is **{{.RepoInfo.ForgeKind}}** ({{.RepoInfo.URL}}), not GitHub.
Use `fj` (CLI) or `smith` MCP tools for issues and pull requests — do NOT use `gh`
and do NOT open issues or PRs on GitHub. If a GitHub mirror exists it is read-only:
push, file issues, and open PRs against the forge URL above.
{{- end}}

Because there is no managed worktree here, the worktree-session conventions do
NOT apply: you are working on the checkout's current branch directly, and
branch hygiene is yours (and the user's) to manage, not spinclass's.

## Merging and closing

`mcp__spinclass__merge-this-session` here runs the `[hooks].pre-merge` gate
against the checkout's current `HEAD` and then `git push` — there is no rebase
and no worktree teardown (you are already on the branch). `sc close` drops only
this session's tracking state; it never touches the checkout.

## Background jobs (merge/check)

When deciding between the synchronous `merge-this-session` /
`check-this-session` and their `-async` twins, **consult your task
list**: if it holds pending or in-progress items beyond the merge
itself, go async — make progress on them while the pre-merge hook
runs, and the `[clown-job]` wake will interrupt you with the result.
If the board is empty and you are attended, the synchronous tool is
fine. If you are unattended (a spawned or dontAsk session), go async
and end your turn: the blocking tool's client request may give up on a
loaded host (a 900 s limit has been seen) while the merge still lands,
and no notice is sent; if a blocking call does time out, do NOT re-run
it, check origin first. The wake re-invokes you when an async job
finishes.

Never poll in a tight loop. If you went async and ran out of other
work with the job near completion, ringmaster's `job_wait` (with the
job id the async tool returned) blocks for the result; inspect on
demand with ringmaster's `job_status` / `job_read`. For a job with
real time remaining, end your turn and let the wake arrive.
